   "daf": "22a",
   "sentenceId": 18,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: אִם הָיָה דֶּרֶךְ רְשׁוּת הָרַבִּים מַפְסַקְתָּן — יְסַלְּקֶנָּה לִצְדָדִין. וַחֲכָמִים אוֹמְרִים: אֵינוֹ צָרִיךְ.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «Rabbi Yehuda says: If the path of the public domain passes through» the area of the upright boards surrounding a well «and obstructs it, one must divert» the path «to the sides,» so that the public will circumvent the enclosed area; otherwise, the partition is invalid and the enclosed area cannot be regarded as a private domain. «And the Rabbis say: One need not» divert the path of the public domain, for the partition is valid even if many people pass through it."
  }
 ],
